# No Auto Commit

Never create a git commit unless the user explicitly asks to commit.

- Writing or editing files is fine
- Do not run `git add` / `git commit` on your own
- Do not treat "push", "check status", or "are there uncommitted changes" as permission to commit
- Only commit when the user clearly says to commit (or equivalent, like "提交这些改动")
